+# Sealed source-registry metadata fixtures
+
+RegistryFrame.mori and REGISTRY-EXPECTED.json are byte-exact copies from the additional independent distinct-reference companion frozen at3b961ce15f9be28ae0f2c5e6d611efc9ee1f01b1cf2d097a909a9296d8eca8d3. Its provenance discloses prior arithmetic/source-admission finding exposure. The semantic SET stays conditional; it is not a backend ordering/cardinality/ABI/context/hash/financial or native oracle. The original conflicting-scale packet c46e0389... remains unchanged.
+
+Core2Registry.mori and CORE2-REGISTRY-EXPECTED.json were separately specified from literal source identities before candidate code/tests. Their author inspected existing code; they are ordinary nonfinancial source-derived expectations, not a blind financial oracle. No implementation output or evaluator produced either expected set.
+
+The positive tests call only load/load_v3 and the metadata accessor. They compare complete identities as SETS, preserve the full Program/plan/hash metadata, and mutate detached owned results to check that a new query is unchanged. They execute no financial transition, start/resume, scenario, backend, SDK, VM, proof, key or ledger operation. No new invalid-input/security policy test is introduced.
+
+This fixture addition does not adopt the broken fullQ1 draft, wire a compiler consumer or choose registry bounds/context/artifact/native contracts. Source checks remain UNRUN in the external candidate preparation; root separately owns integration, fresh source audit and any actual checks.
